From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:04:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nb/intel/haswell: Use PCH backlight duty cycle for ACPI

The ACPI brightness methods read and write the PWM duty cycle at
INTEL_GMA_BCLV_OFFSET and the PWM period at INTEL_GMA_BCLM_OFFSET.
Haswell overrides the duty cycle offset with 0x48254 (BLC_PWM_CPU_CTL),
the Sandy Bridge location, while the period is read from the default
0xc8256, the upper half of BLC_PWM_PCH_CTL2.

With a Lynx Point PCH the backlight PWM runs in PCH override mode: the
GMA init sets BLM_PCH_OVERRIDE_ENABLE, and so does the Linux driver,
which writes the duty cycle to BLC_PWM_PCH_CTL2[15:0] only. Nothing
writes BLC_PWM_CPU_CTL, so _BQC computes the current level from a stale
register and reports the lowest level, and the legacy _BCM fallback
writes to a register that has no effect. Brightness keys handled by the
firmware then step relative to the lowest level as well.

Drop the override, so that the default 0xc8254 (BLC_PWM_PCH_CTL2[15:0])
is used, like on Broadwell.

TEST=Built for lenovo/w541. Not tested on hardware yet: with the
acpi_video backlight, the value read from actual_brightness must follow
the level written to brightness.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig
index 6015c3170..11950198a 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig
@@ -127,9 +127,6 @@ config RO_REGION_ONLY
 	depends on VBOOT
 	default "mrc.bin"
 
-config INTEL_GMA_BCLV_OFFSET
-	default 0x48254
-
 config ENABLE_DDR_2X_REFRESH
 	bool "Enable DRAM Refresh 2x support"
 	default n
